  siteDistance: {x: 35, y: 70}
  siteText: 'At the Black Pool''s edge a door of old stone leans out of the water, open on nothing. The fen runs out of it: this is where his wrong doors opened, and what came through drowned the marsh. A Hearth Ember set in its sill would close it.'
  artwork: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 390f841f37daf3f4c96afdc728c3344d, type: 3}
  onStart: []
  choices:
  - label: Set a Hearth Ember in it
    detail: It will close, and what is still on the other side will not like it.
    cost:
    - item: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3bc5c06eef042084b9fc28865091670b, type: 2}
      amount: 1
    result: The ember takes in the wet stone like a coal in tinder. The door grinds shut, and the water round it boils with what was coming.
    outcomes:
